{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"11 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,24.305,3.651,3.268,"Tega Industries"],[13.889,14.731,27.336,2.373,2.124,"Tenfold revenue, no profit yet"],[13.889,20.845,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Tega’s first full quarter with Molycop shows what the acquisition bought and"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"what it costs. Q2 FY27 revenue of ₹4,254 cr was 10.5 times a year earlier and"],[13.889,23.733,52.934,1.809,1.634,"adjusted EBITDA was ₹608 cr. Depreciation then took ₹169 cr, finance costs"],[13.889,25.177,52.936,1.809,1.634,"₹292 cr, one-off deal costs ₹78 cr and tax ₹132 cr, leaving a loss of ₹59 cr. Net"],[13.889,26.621,52.964,1.809,1.634,"debt is ₹10,461 cr, 4.3x annualised EBITDA, including c.₹2,600 cr of"],[13.889,28.065,52.936,1.809,1.634,"redeemable preference shares. The legacy liner business grew income 18%, yet"],[13.889,29.509,49.489,1.809,1.634,"its adjusted PAT fell 65% to ₹16 cr after ₹30 cr of acquisition-loan interest."],[13.889,31.995,52.931,1.809,1.634,"1) Molycop: we take H2 EBITDA at ₹479 cr a quarter, midway between Q2"],[13.889,33.439,52.987,1.809,1.634,"(₹514 cr) and the August guidance rate, then 3% volume growth and USD 18m"],[13.889,34.883,52.931,1.809,1.634,"of synergies by FY29E (USD 20m guided). 2) Legacy consumables grow 15% a"],[13.889,36.328,52.934,1.809,1.634,"year, as guided, at a 21-22% margin. 3) Tax is the swing factor: Molycop’s"],[13.889,37.772,52.936,1.809,1.634,"adjusted tax was 31% of EBIT in June-September, as holding-level interest"],[13.889,39.216,52.961,1.809,1.634,"earned almost no shield; we assume 27% and 25% in FY28-29E. Adjusted EPS"],[13.889,40.684,52.936,1.809,1.634,"is then ₹14.3, ₹38.9 and ₹66.3 for FY27-29E. Taxed at 30% of pre-tax profit"],[13.889,42.128,51.787,1.809,1.634,"instead, FY28E EPS would be ₹66.5, near the ₹69.6 consensus (range ₹43-94)."],[13.889,44.59,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹1,680 averages two methods. Sum of the parts gives"],[13.889,46.034,52.951,1.809,1.634,"₹1,990: legacy Tega at 16.2x forward EBITDA (peer median: AIA Engineering,"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Metso, Weir, FLSmidth) and Molycop at the 7.9x paid in June, less net debt and"],[13.889,48.946,52.966,1.809,1.634,"Apollo’s 15.8%. A ten-year FCFE DCF (13% cost of equity, 5.5% terminal"],[13.889,50.39,52.931,1.809,1.634,"growth) gives ₹1,365, as multiples ignore the interest and tax leak. Each turn on"],[13.889,51.834,52.951,1.809,1.634,"Molycop’s multiple is worth ₹246 a share; today’s price implies 7.6x FY28E."],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"We rate the shares Neutral (ladder: −5% to +15%). Upside risks: refinancing the"],[13.889,54.722,52.931,1.809,1.634,"preference shares, a lower tax rate. Downside: Chinese grinding-media"],[13.889,56.167,26.45,1.809,1.634,"competition, a copper or gold downturn."],[13.889,58.654,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[14.451,68.023,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,400"],[14.451,66.066,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,600"],[14.451,64.109,2.306,1.022,0.915,"1,800"],[14.451,62.152,2.306,1.022,0.915,"2,000"],[14.451,60.195,2.306,1.022,0.915,"2,200"],[18.454,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[23.078,68.717,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.865,68.717,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.618,68.717,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.975,69.888,2.57,1.275,1.111,"Tega ("],[21.548,69.914,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.161,69.888,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.245,69.888,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.5,71.048,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.981,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.066,71.048,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.048,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.114,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[19.244,72.114,3.148,1.387,1.209,"-13.9%"],[24.174,72.114,3.148,1.387,1.209,"-13.3%"],[29.147,72.114,2.26,1.387,1.209,"2.0%"],[33.19,72.114,3.148,1.387,1.209,"-12.7%"],[1